# No lab configuration in operator UI (hard rule)

Operator directive (Phil, 2026-08-08), verbatim:

> **NEVER put internal lab configuration rules in UI visible to users or
> administrators. Agent/operator dialogs are not part of the product UI.
> Only generic product instructions in SPA/configurator UI — never disclose
> lab configuration (phil rotation bans, BEAVIS2, liebsoft/lanicu, seed-dev,
> Path 2 Live lab CLI recipes, SoftHSM PINs, Mailpit lab wiring, "lab
> default", etc.). Lab runbooks stay in docs/dev and agent prompts.**

**Exception** (Phil, 2026-08-08), narrowed same day:

> **When building seed systems for developers, demo, or production, agents
> or the configurator MAY attach appropriate per-system comments that alert
> the operator for that asset's use case — in product language. Comments
> are data on the system/asset record, shown in inventory lists. They must
> NOT contain lab hostnames, lab account names, "never rotate phil", CLI
> lab recipes, BEAVIS2, SoftHSM PINs, Mailpit, seed-dev flags, AI/agent
> thinking, or internal delivery status jargon meant for engineers.**

**Browser-source clarification** (Phil, 2026-08-08):

> **The ban applies to what the user sees AND to UI source that ships to
> the browser** (admin SPA `ui/src/` and anything bundled into the client
> JS). Do not leave lab configuration strings, lab identity names, CLI lab
> recipes, or AI/agent thinking in React/TS/JS string literals, defaults,
> comments a bundler might keep, i18n catalogs, or fixtures imported by
> the SPA.

## The rule

> **The ban applies to (1) everything an operator can see at runtime and
> (2) every byte of admin-SPA / client UI source that ships in the browser
> bundle — not OT-only, not Alert-only, not "hidden behind a feature
> flag." Runtime chrome, operator-visible data fields, and browser-shipped
> source must never leak (a) internal lab configuration information, or
> (b) information about what the AI is thinking.**

Cursor chat, `.cursor/rules`, agent skills, and Task prompts are **not**
product UI — lab SOP and agent plans belong there and in `docs/dev`.
Nothing from that surface is copied into browser-shipped source, API
payloads meant as UI chrome, or seeded fields operators read.

## Do not leak (two classes)

| Class | Forbidden examples (non-exhaustive) |
| --- | --- |
| **(a) Internal lab configuration** | BEAVIS2 / Beavis2 / `192.168.55.197`; liebsoft / lanicu; "never rotate phil"; seed-dev / `db-init --confirm` / Restore-Beavis2Lab; Path 2 Live / wave labels; lab CLI recipes (`ot-credentials rotate-job …`); SoftHSM PINs / slots / Fix-LabSoftHsmLibraryPath; Mailpit / `127.0.0.1:1025` / `:8025`; "(lab default)", "lab only", "on lab hosts" |
| **(b) What the AI is thinking** | Agent plans; model reasoning; "as an AI"; internal slice status; parent/child agent chatter; "TODO for agents"; Cursor/session notes; delivery jargon meant for engineers ("Phase 4.0 done", "blocked on sibling", "parent will resume") |

Both classes are forbidden in **runtime chrome**, **operator-visible
data**, and **browser-shipped UI source**.

## Scope

| Surface | May contain lab config or AI thinking? |
| --- | --- |
| Admin SPA runtime (banners, chips, tooltips, helperText, placeholders, empty states, menus) | **No** |
| Admin SPA **source** shipping to the browser: `pim-offline-server/ui/src/**` and any path imported into the client bundle — string literals, defaults, i18n catalogs, fixtures, retained comments | **No** |
| Sibling client UI bundling to the browser (Tauri/web shells under product `src/` that ship) | **No** |
| Win32 / Tauri configurators, elevate helpers, launchers, About text | **No** |
| Customer-facing CLI `--help` / operator messages | **No** |
| API error / OpenAPI text returned into the UI as chrome | **No** |
| Assessment Binder export / section text operators read | **No** |
| Inventory / system / asset `comment`, notes, description, and any other operator-visible data field | **No** for lab config or AI thinking; **Yes** for product-language use-case comments (exception below) |
| `docs/dev/**`, `.cursor/rules/**`, agent skills, Task prompts | **Yes** — not product UI / not browser bundle |
| Playwright / e2e under `ui/e2e/**` (not imported by `ui/src`) | **Yes** — test-only; never import those fixtures into the SPA |
| Lab PowerShell under `scripts/` | **Yes** — operator/agent tooling |
| Server-only lab seed modules | **Yes**, if they **never** serialize instructional lab SOP into API payloads meant as UI chrome; seed **comments** still follow the narrow exception |

Hiding a string behind `import.meta.env.DEV`, a dead branch, or a "lab
only" comment in `ui/src` does **not** satisfy this rule — if it is in
browser-shipped source, it is forbidden.

## Per-system comment exception (narrow)

Operators and seed builders **may** set a `comment` (or equivalent) that
describes the **asset use case for the operator/customer** in plain
product language. Lists may show that field. That is not a license to
smuggle lab SOP or agent notes into the database or into SPA defaults.

| Comment content | Status |
| --- | --- |
| Asset role / purpose in product words | **Allowed** |
| Caution about personal admin accounts in generic terms | **Allowed** |
| Lab hostnames, lab accounts, phil bans, CLI lab recipes, BEAVIS2, SoftHSM PINs, Mailpit, seed-dev flags | **Forbidden** (even in comments / even in `ui/src` defaults) |
| AI/agent thinking, slice status, Cursor notes, engineer delivery jargon | **Forbidden** (even in source comments that ship) |
| Paste of agent dialog or private lab SOP into any seed profile | **Forbidden** |

Dev/demo/prod seeds alike: comments stay use-case clean. Dev seeds may say
the asset is for discovery drills; they still must not name the lab or the
agent.

## Required agent behavior

1. Before writing **any** operator-visible string, seed field, or `ui/src`
   (or other client-bundled) literal, ask: is this lab configuration, or
   agent/AI thinking? If yes → `docs/dev` or Cursor rules only.
2. Do not "park" lab recipes in SPA comments, i18n keys, or unused
   constants "for developers" — View Source and source maps expose them.
3. When seeding comments, describe only what the **operator** needs about
   that asset's use case, in product language.
4. Keep lab identity and host rules in
   [`beavis2-lab-hard-rules.mdc`](beavis2-lab-hard-rules.mdc) and lab
   scripts — never paste them into UI source or inventory fields.
5. Product honesty
   ([`compliance-claims-honesty.mdc`](compliance-claims-honesty.mdc)) and
   credibility
   ([`operator-ui-credibility.mdc`](operator-ui-credibility.mdc)) still
   bind: lab jargon and AI meta-talk in the product are P0 defects.
6. Mirror this rule to `core-assets/.cursor/rules/` in the same change set
   ([`auto-commit-push.mdc`](auto-commit-push.mdc)).

## Worked violation → fix

**Bad** — OT Inventory Rotate panel, lab runbook in UI *and* in `ui/src`
string literals:

```text
Path 2 Live (lab): ot-credentials rotate-job --custody key-manager…
Lab only — never rotate phil. Selected asset: (lab default)
```

**Good** — generic product chrome / source:

```text
Rotate credentials for the selected asset. Leave the old password empty
to rotate the password currently in effect. Prefer a dedicated service
account — do not use personal administrator accounts for rotation drills.
```

**Bad comment** (lab + AI thinking in a visible data field):
`Path 2 Live lab — agent will rotate via ot-credentials…`

**Good comment** (asset use case in product language):
`Modbus TCP simulator used for discovery and credential drills.`

Lab CLI recipes, BEAVIS2, phil bans, SoftHSM/Mailpit wiring, and agent
plans stay in `docs/dev`, server-only seed modules (without SOP-as-chrome
payloads), and agent prompts — not in `ui/src` or any client bundle.

